Eden's base userland has no realpath (it lives in GNU coreutils).  Use
readlink -f instead, which sbase provides and behaves the same for the
existing paths distrobox resolves.  findmnt/nsenter are not required on
the host: the only findmnt call is an optional read-only mount check that
degrades to the read-write mount path, and nsenter is used inside the
container only.

